### Database Queries (Laravel Eloquent)

```php
// ✅ GOOD: Select only needed columns
$markets = Market::select(['id', 'name', 'status'])
    ->where('status', 'active')
    ->limit(10)
    ->get();

// ✅ GOOD: Eager loading to prevent N+1
$markets = Market::with(['creator:id,name', 'options'])
    ->where('status', 'active')
    ->get();

// ❌ BAD: Select everything (loads unnecessary columns)
$markets = Market::all();

// ❌ BAD: N+1 query problem
$markets = Market::all();
foreach ($markets as $market) {
    echo $market->creator->name; // N queries!
}
```

## Testing Standards

### PestPHP Test Structure (Backend)

```php
// ✅ GOOD: Clear test with AAA pattern
it('creates a market with options', function () {
    // Arrange
    $user = User::factory()->create();
    $data = [
        'name' => 'Election 2024',
        'description' => 'Presidential election market',
        'category' => 'politics',
        'options' => [
            ['name' => 'Candidate A'],
            ['name' => 'Candidate B'],
        ]
    ];

    // Act
    $response = actingAs($user)->post('/markets', $data);

    // Assert
    $response->assertRedirect();
    expect(Market::count())->toBe(1);
    expect(Market::first()->options)->toHaveCount(2);
});

// ✅ GOOD: Test with authorization check
it('prevents unauthorized users from deleting markets', function () {
    $market = Market::factory()->create();
    $otherUser = User::factory()->create();

    actingAs($otherUser)
        ->delete("/markets/{$market->id}")
        ->assertForbidden();

    expect(Market::count())->toBe(1);
});
```

