## Code Smell Detection

Watch for these anti-patterns:

### 1. Long Functions/Methods

```php
// ❌ BAD: Controller method > 50 lines
public function store(Request $request)
{
    // 100 lines of business logic, validation, database operations
}

// ✅ GOOD: Extract to service layer
public function store(StoreMarketRequest $request): RedirectResponse
{
    $market = $this->marketService->create($request->validated());
    return redirect()->route('markets.show', $market);
}
```

### 2. Deep Nesting

```php
// ❌ BAD: 5+ levels of nesting
if ($user) {
    if ($user->is_admin) {
        if ($market) {
            if ($market->isActive()) {
                if (Gate::allows('update', $market)) {
                    // Do something
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Early returns
if (!$user) {
    abort(401);
}

if (!$user->is_admin) {
    abort(403);
}

if (!$market || !$market->isActive()) {
    abort(404);
}

Gate::authorize('update', $market);

// Do something
```

### 3. Magic Numbers

```php
// ❌ BAD: Unexplained numbers
if ($retryCount > 3) { }
sleep(5);

// ✅ GOOD: Named constants
private const MAX_RETRIES = 3;
private const RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS = 5;

if ($retryCount > self::MAX_RETRIES) { }
sleep(self::RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS);
```

### 4. Missing Type Declarations

```php
// ❌ BAD: No types (PHP 8.2+)
public function calculateTotal($items)
{
    return array_sum($items);
}

// ✅ GOOD: Full type declarations
public function calculateTotal(array $items): float
{
    return array_sum($items);
}
```

### 5. Fat Models

```php
// ❌ BAD: Model with business logic (>200 lines)
class Market extends Model
{
    // 50 methods with complex business logic
}

// ✅ GOOD: Extract to service or repository
class Market extends Model
{
    // Only relationships, scopes, accessors, mutators
}

class MarketService
{
    // Business logic here
}
```

## Laravel-Specific Best Practices

### 1. Use Route Model Binding

```php
// ✅ GOOD: Automatic model resolution
public function show(Market $market): Response
{
    return Inertia::render('Markets/Show', compact('market'));
}

// ❌ BAD: Manual lookup
public function show($id)
{
    $market = Market::findOrFail($id);
    return Inertia::render('Markets/Show', compact('market'));
}
```

### 2. Use Policies for Authorization

```php
// ✅ GOOD: Policy check
public function update(UpdateMarketRequest $request, Market $market): RedirectResponse
{
    $this->authorize('update', $market);

    $market->update($request->validated());
    return back();
}

// ❌ BAD: Manual permission check
public function update(Request $request, Market $market)
{
    if ($market->creator_id !== auth()->id()) {
        abort(403);
    }
}
```

### 3. Use Database Transactions

```php
// ✅ GOOD: Transaction for multi-step operations
public function create(array $data): Market
{
    return DB::transaction(function () use ($data) {
        $market = Market::create($data);
        $market->options()->createMany($data['options']);
        return $market;
    });
}

// ❌ BAD: No transaction protection
public function create(array $data)
{
    $market = Market::create($data);
    $market->options()->createMany($data['options']); // Could fail!
    return $market;
}
```

**Remember**: Code quality is not negotiable. Clear, maintainable code enables rapid development and confident refactoring.

**Stack**: Laravel 12 (PHP 8.2+) + Vue 3 Options API + Inertia.js 2 + MySQL 8 + TypeScript
